{
  "_comment": [
    "Template only, and named so Codex cannot mistake it for the real thing.",
    "`agentgit install` writes hooks.json beside it, with the NODE, TRACK, SPINE,",
    "HUB and DESKTOP placeholders replaced by absolute paths on this machine. Codex",
    "performs no command substitution and does not resolve a POSIX-style relative",
    "script path on Windows, so absolute paths are the only form that works everywhere.",
    "That is why hooks.json is gitignored and this template is not.",
    "",
    "Matchers are deliberately broad. The hook script classifies the tool itself",
    "and ignores anything that cannot change a file, so a tool Codex renames or",
    "adds still gets recorded instead of silently dropping out of the ledger.",
    "",
    "Two scripts, on purpose, with different costs and different jobs:",
    "  - track.mjs records one ledger line. It runs on every tool call and does no",
    "    analysis at all.",
    "  - spine.mjs makes sure one daemon is watching this workspace, and says nothing.",
    "    It runs at session start and on each prompt, because the daemon is what writes",
    "    the projection hub.mjs reads: without it the push channel is permanently silent.",
    "  - hub.mjs pushes the hub's ruling into the session. It reads one small file",
    "    the daemon writes and never reads the ledger, so its cost does not grow with",
    "    the workspace. It is a second handler rather than a separate event so both",
    "    scripts see the same payload, and track.mjs stays first so recording can",
    "    never be delayed by anything the hub does.",
    "  - desktop.mjs speaks at the three moments before anything is in flight: a repository",
    "    that has not opted in is offered the chance to (remembered on the machine, never in",
    "    the repository), an opted-in workspace is offered a pinned coordination task, and a",
    "    message that starts with /agentgit is carried out rather than asked about - because",
    "    the command is itself the explicit user request the host requires. A plugin cannot",
    "    create a Codex task, so the two offers are the whole of what a hook can do here,",
    "    and every one of the three is remembered so none of them becomes a nag.",
    "",
    "The order on SessionStart and UserPromptSubmit is track, spine, hub, desktop: record",
    "first, then make sure there is something to rule, then read the ruling, and only then",
    "consider asking the user a question. desktop.mjs can inject context but changes no",
    "coordination state - the only thing it writes is the record of a question it asked,",
    "and never the ledger - so it goes last: nothing it does may delay the three above it.",
    "spine.mjs and desktop.mjs are deliberately absent from PreToolUse: starting a daemon",
    "and asking a question are both things that have no business between an agent and its",
    "next edit.",
    "",
    "The hub handler on PreToolUse is narrowed to file edits. A ruling is only worth",
    "interrupting a write with when the write is about the ground it rules on, and",
    "the host's own event schema is what says which tools those are."
  ],
  "hooks": {
    "SessionStart": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{TRACK}}\"" },
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{SPINE}}\"" },
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{HUB}}\"" },
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{DESKTOP}}\"" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "UserPromptSubmit": [
      {
        "hooks": [
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{TRACK}}\"" },
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{SPINE}}\"" },
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{HUB}}\"" },
          { "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{DESKTOP}}\"" }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "PreToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": ".*",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{TRACK}}\"" }]
      },
      {
        "matcher": "apply_patch|Edit|Write",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{HUB}}\"" }]
      }
    ],
    "PostToolUse": [
      {
        "matcher": ".*",
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{TRACK}}\"" }]
      }
    ],
    "Stop": [
      {
        "hooks": [{ "type": "command", "command": "\"{{NODE}}\" \"{{TRACK}}\"" }]
      }
    ]
  }
}
